  "description": "ARULIK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H82 N7 O30 Tb5,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 4 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.741-3.850 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.41-108.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C73H86N7O31Tb5.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
